{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"a4641d440d74bdaf72a6ec418dc7e1cf3b766bfd733d7cfae2272c00a2fa8fc0","digest":{"component_or_area":"completion floor unit tests","key_entities":["test_completion_floor_e2e.py","test_non_regression_floor_is_review_only","_apply_completion_floor_to_verdict","attest._MANIFEST_PREFIX","inspect.getsource"],"problem_keywords":["test coverage","purity contract","source-based validation","false positive","completion floor","side-effect detection","finding conservation","mutation detection"],"propositions":["The current source-token test uses inspect.getsource to detect absence of signing/transition keywords, which is vacuous against pure functions and evadable via refactoring.","The floor's behavioral intent (findings conservation and no attestation side-output) is not verified by scanning source code; a pure verdict transform can only be tested via observable state before/after the call.","The floor must not fabricate, silently drop, or rewrite findings — the multiset of finding ids across advisory and dropped lists must remain identical before and after the transformation.","The floor must not add signature, attestation, or attestations keys to the verdict, only the dropped list and coverage narrowing annotations.","The floor must not mutate its input cmap or finding content dicts by reference or value — it re-partitions list membership only."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785820754302462746,"uuid":"5e26e722-1a15-4031-8578-00a66f1b5c4d"}